<InfoPanel Title="Prototype Boundaries" Subtitle="What the current project is and is not.">
    <ChildContent>
        <div class="of-review-proof-grid">
            <div class="of-review-proof-card">
                <strong>Current Demo</strong>
                <span>Runs as a local Blazor/SQLite demo app with local file storage under the configured upload path.</span>
            </div>

            <div class="of-review-proof-card">
                <strong>Workflow Scope</strong>
                <span>Tracks workflow metadata, ownership, status, due dates, notes, evidence, history, and reports.</span>
            </div>

            <div class="of-review-proof-card">
                <strong>Not Live Yet</strong>
                <span>Does not use live authentication, live Microsoft Lists, SharePoint storage, Teams, or Outlook notifications yet.</span>
            </div>

            <div class="of-review-proof-card">
                <strong>Not Production Storage Yet</strong>
                <span>Does not store real production business documents and does not enforce production audit retention rules yet.</span>
            </div>

            <div class="of-review-proof-card">
                <strong>Week 3 Foundation</strong>
                <span>Maps local prototype data and local files to Microsoft Lists/SharePoint-ready structures.</span>
            </div>

            <div class="of-review-proof-card">
                <strong>Week 4 Direction</strong>
                <span>Use a test tenant to build Microsoft 365 auth, SharePoint storage, Power Automate, and production-style permissions.</span>
            </div>
        </div>
    </ChildContent>
</InfoPanel>

<GuidanceNote Title="Reviewer Notes" Icon="💡" Tone="info">
    <ul>
        <li>Judge this as a production-shaped prototype, not a fully deployed SaaS product.</li>
        <li>The important proof is the workflow thinking: capture, ownership, evidence, reporting, and traceability.</li>
        <li>The evidence layer is intentionally provider-independent so local storage can be replaced by SharePoint later.</li>
        <li>The app now shows management value, not just CRUD screens.</li>
        <li>Week 4 should focus on Microsoft 365 implementation, authentication, permissions, deployment, and production documentation.</li>
    </ul>
</GuidanceNote>